### WCF Appointment Service REST API Tests
### Base URL - Update the port number to match your local development server
@baseUrl = http://localhost:63124
@serviceUrl = {{baseUrl}}/AppointmentService.svc

### 1. Get All Appointments
GET {{serviceUrl}}/appointments
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. Get Specific Appointment by ID
GET {{serviceUrl}}/appointments/1
Accept: application/json

###

### 3. Get Appointment by ID 2
GET {{serviceUrl}}/appointments/2
Accept: application/json

###

### 4. Create New Appointment - Basic
POST {{serviceUrl}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "Title": "Follow-up Consultation",
  "Description": "Follow-up appointment for test results review",
  "AppointmentDate": "2024-12-20T10:00:00",
  "Location": "Room 303",
  "PatientName": "Michael Johnson",
  "DoctorName": "Dr. Williams",
  "DurationMinutes": 30
}

###

### 5. Create New Appointment - Detailed
POST {{serviceUrl}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "Title": "Cardiology Appointment",
  "Description": "Annual heart health checkup and EKG",
  "AppointmentDate": "2024-12-25T14:30:00",
  "Location": "Cardiology Department - Room 501",
  "PatientName": "Sarah Davis",
  "DoctorName": "Dr. Anderson",
  "DurationMinutes": 60
}

###

### 6. Create New Appointment - Emergency
POST {{serviceUrl}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "Title": "Emergency Consultation",
  "Description": "Urgent care visit for acute symptoms",
  "AppointmentDate": "2024-12-15T09:00:00",
  "Location": "Emergency Room",
  "PatientName": "Robert Brown",
  "DoctorName": "Dr. Martinez",
  "DurationMinutes": 45
}

###

### 7. Test Invalid Request - Missing Title (Should return Bad Request)
POST {{serviceUrl}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "Description": "This should fail - missing title",
  "AppointmentDate": "2024-12-20T10:00:00",
  "Location": "Room 303",
  "PatientName": "Test Patient",
  "DoctorName": "Dr. Test",
  "DurationMinutes": 30
}

###

### 8. Test Invalid Request - Missing Patient Name (Should return Bad Request)
POST {{serviceUrl}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "Title": "Test Appointment",
  "Description": "This should fail - missing patient name",
  "AppointmentDate": "2024-12-20T10:00:00",
  "Location": "Room 303",
  "DoctorName": "Dr. Test",
  "DurationMinutes": 30
}

###

### 9. Get Non-existent Appointment (Should return null or 404)
GET {{serviceUrl}}/appointments/999
Accept: application/json

###

### Alternative: Using different port numbers (Update as needed)
# @baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
# @baseUrl = http://localhost:44300
# @baseUrl = https://localhost:44300

### NOTES:
### 1. Update the @baseUrl variable with your actual development server URL and port
### 2. The service URL is: {baseUrl}/AppointmentService.svc
### 3. Endpoints:
###    - GET  /appointments      : Get all appointments
###    - GET  /appointments/{id} : Get appointment by ID
###    - POST /appointments      : Create new appointment
### 4. To run tests:
###    - Click "Send Request" above each request
###    - Or use Ctrl+Alt+R (Windows) / Cmd+Alt+R (Mac) when cursor is on the request
